","member":"316","deposited":{"date-parts":[[2024,8,20]],"date-time":"2024-08-20T03:42:17Z","timestamp":1724125337000},"score":30.877407,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/pubs.acs.org\/doi\/suppl\/10.1021\/acs.analchem.3c04479\/suppl_file\/ac3c04479_si_003.xlsx"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[null]]},"references-count":0,"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1021\/acs.analchem.3c04479.s003","relation":{"is-component-of":[{"id-type":"doi","id":"10.1021\/acs.analchem.3c04479","asserted-by":"object"}]}},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,2,26]],"date-time":"2026-02-26T16:37:49Z","timestamp":1772123869406,"version":"3.50.1"},"description":"Supplemental Information for 10.1021\/acs.analchem.3c04479","reference-count":0,"publisher":"American Chemical Society (ACS)","content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"DOI":"10.1021\/acs.analchem.3c04479.s001","type":"component","created":{"date-parts":[[2024,8,5]],"date-time":"2024-08-05T18:33:17Z","timestamp":1722882797000},"source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["Quantitative Comparison of Deparaffinization, Rehydration and Extraction Methods for FFPE Tissue Proteomics and Phosphoproteomics"],"prefix":"10.1021","member":"316","deposited":{"date-parts":[[2024,8,20]],"date-time":"2024-08-20T03:42:17Z","timestamp":1724125337000},"score":30.757168,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/pubs.acs.org\/doi\/suppl\/10.1021\/acs.analchem.3c04479\/suppl_file\/ac3c04479_si_001.pdf"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[null]]},"references-count":0,"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1021\/acs.analchem.3c04479.s001","relation":{"is-component-of":[{"id-type":"doi","id":"10.1021\/acs.analchem.3c04479","asserted-by":"object"}]}},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,2,26]],"date-time":"2026-02-26T16:38:20Z","timestamp":1772123900510,"version":"3.50.1"},"description":"Supplemental Information for 10.1021\/acs.analchem.3c04479","reference-count":0,"publisher":"American Chemical Society (ACS)","content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"DOI":"10.1021\/acs.analchem.3c04479.s004","type":"component","created":{"date-parts":[[2024,8,5]],"date-time":"2024-08-05T18:33:17Z","timestamp":1722882797000},"source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["Quantitative Comparison of Deparaffinization, Rehydration and Extraction Methods for FFPE Tissue Proteomics and Phosphoproteomics"],"prefix":"10.1021","member":"316","deposited":{"date-parts":[[2024,8,20]],"date-time":"2024-08-20T03:42:18Z","timestamp":1724125338000},"score":30.754135,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/pubs.acs.org\/doi\/suppl\/10.1021\/acs.analchem.3c04479\/suppl_file\/ac3c04479_si_004.xlsx"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[null]]},"references-count":0,"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1021\/acs.analchem.3c04479.s004","relation":{"is-component-of":[{"id-type":"doi","id":"10.1021\/acs.analchem.3c04479","asserted-by":"object"}]}},{"institution":[{"name":"bioRxiv"}],"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,1,15]],"date-time":"2026-01-15T19:43:23Z","timestamp":1768506203056,"version":"3.49.0"},"posted":{"date-parts":[[2023,5,4]]},"group-title":"Cell Biology","reference-count":68,"publisher":"openRxiv","content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"accepted":{"date-parts":[[2023,5,4]]},"abstract":"<jats:title>Abstract<\/jats:title>\n                <jats:p>\n                  Tardigrades can survive hostile environments such as desiccation by adopting a state of anhydrobiosis. Numerous tardigrade species have been described thus far, and recent genome and transcriptome analyses revealed that several distinct strategies were employed to cope with harsh environments depending on the evolutionary lineages. Detailed analyses at the cellular and subcellular levels are essential to complete these data. In this work, we analyzed a tardigrade species that can withstand rapid dehydration,\n                  <jats:italic>Ramazzottius varieornatus<\/jats:italic>\n                  . Surprisingly, we noted an absence of the anhydrobiotic-specific extracellular structure previously described for the\n                  <jats:italic>Hypsibius exemplaris<\/jats:italic>\n                  species. Both\n                  <jats:italic>Ramazzottius varieornatus<\/jats:italic>\n                  and\n                  <jats:italic>Hypsibius exemplaris<\/jats:italic>\n                  belong to the same evolutionary class of Eutardigrada. Nevertheless, our observations reveal discrepancies in the anhydrobiosis mechanisms between these two species. Interestingly, these discrepancies are correlated with their variations in dehydration resistance.\n                <\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1101\/2023.05.03.539216","type":"posted-content","created":{"date-parts":[[2023,5,4]],"date-time":"2023-05-04T20:40:30Z","timestamp":1683232830000},"source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["A comparative ultrastructure study of the tardigrade\n                  <i>Ramazzottius varieornatus<\/i>\n                  in the hydrated state, after desiccation and during the process of rehydration"],"prefix":"10.64898","author":[{"given":"Simon","family":"Galas","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Emilie","family":"Le Goff","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Chantal","family":"Cazevieille","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Akihiro","family":"Tanaka","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Pierre","family":"Cuq","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Stephen","family":"Baghdiguian","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Takekazu","family":"Kunieda","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"giv